es plurielles Culture, science, société Culture, science, société Activités, expos et événements Cours, conférences et débats Médias et jeux Ateliers scolaires et ressources didactiques Patrimoine et musées Interlocuteurs-contacts Actus et Agenda Dans la même rubrique Vie sur les campus Se préparer et réussir ses études Premières choses à faire Aides et accompagnement S'impliquer et s'informer Accès aux auditoires et campus Santé et bien-être Restaurants et commerces Sport Culture Logement Bibliothèques Biodiversité Secours, sécurité Prévention et protection S'engager Soutenir l'ULB ULB solidaire Travailler et collaborer Emplois académiques et scientifiques Offres d'emploi administratif, technique, de gestion et spécialisé Pourquoi travailler à l'ULB ? Job étudiant InfOR-emploi Espace entreprises L'ULB et l'École InfOR-Études ULB E.COL.E L'université des enseignants Les écoles plurielles Culture, science, société Activités, expos et événements Cours, conférences et débats Médias et jeux Ateliers scolaires et ressources didactiques Patrimoine et musées Interlocuteurs-contacts Actus et Agenda Accueil FR L'ULB et vous Travailler et collaborer Emplois académiques et scientifiques Imprimer Partager Partager cette page Envoyer par email Facebook Twitter Linkedin Viadeo Faculté de Médecine Corps académique Il n'y a pas de vacance dans ce corps actuellement. Corps scientifique 26-S151 - Assistant.e chargé.e d'exercices 60h en physiologie et physiopathologie Faculté de Médecine Médecine - Professeurs non attachés Domaine :  Sciences médicales Référence : 26-S151 La date limite du dépôt des candidatures est fixée au: 04/09/2026 à midi Lire l'annonce Postuler Voir mon profil Autres offres d'emplois académiques et scientifiques Corps académique Il n'y a pas de vacance dans le corps académique actuellement Cours à pourvoir Réservés aux candidatures internes Il n'y a pas de vacance dans les cours à pourvoir actuellement Corps scientifique Postdoctoral researcher-Cancer biology Faculté de Médecine The Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) at the Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB), led by Panagiotis (Takis) Karras, is seeking motivated researchers to undertake a PhD in cancer research. The candidate will focus on a project to better characterize the drivers of cancer metastasis, profile the inter- and intra-tumor heterogeneity and plasticity combining mouse models and clinical samples. The successful applicant will join the ULB Faculty of Medicine and the Institute Jules Bordet within the campus. Date limite : until the position is filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Full time position for postdoc bioinformatician Faculté de Médecine The Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) at the Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB), led by Panagiotis (Takis) Karras, is seeking for a skilled bioinformatician with experience in single-cell multi-omics. The candidate will focus on projects to better characterize the drivers of cancer metastasis, profile the inter- and intra-tumor heterogeneity and plasticity combining mouse models and clinical samples. Applicants should demonstrate expertise in programming languages (Python and/or R) as well as experience working with high-performance computing clusters. The successful applicant will join the ULB Faculty of Medicine and the Institute Jules Bordet within the campus. Date limite : until the position is filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Full-time PhD Position in mass spectrometry and cancer biology Faculté de Médecine About the laboratory and environment The research unit on kinase addiction and BruProMS (ULB/Erasme Mass Spectrometry and Proteomics Platform) are based at the IRIBHM J.E. Dumont, at the Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB). Our laboratory focuses its research on protein kinase biology, proteomics, phosphoproteomics, with a particular expertise in cell cycle kinases (CDK4, Greatwall/MASTL) and their implication on cancer. The research group is associated with BruProMS, ULB's mass spectrometry and proteomics platform, and partner of the BRUXSOMICS project (FEDER Brussels), an inter-university ULB-VUB multi-omics platform using mass spectrometry. Positions summary We are seeking a motivated PhD student to undertake a doctoral project at the interface of chemical proteomics, mass spectrometry-based (phospho)proteomics, cell biology, and bioinformatics. The candidate will work on a project aiming at developing the necessary tools to measure kinase activity profiles directly from clinical samples and to build a functional atlas of poorly characterized kinases, with the long-term ambition of enabling precision medicine by correlating tumor kinase activity with therapeutic response to kinase inhibitors. Date limite : Until the position is filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Postdoctoral Scientist - Molecular mechanisms of metabolic cell dysfunction associated with protein tyrosine phosphatases Faculté de Médecine The Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory (www.stmlaboratoy.com) led by Dr Esteban Gurzov is seeking highly motivated post-doctoral researchers to explore the pathophysiological mechanisms contributing to metabolic dysfunction. The successful applicant will join the ULB Faculty of Medicine, characterised by an impressive track record in research excellence. Project description: The project will take advantage of human stem cells, diabetes cell models, mouse models, pharmacological approaches and human specimens to determine the molecular mechanisms by which dysfunctional signalling contributes to the development of obesity, diabetes and liver cancer, and to explore novel approaches for combating the pathologies. The Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory provides a world leading environment for creative science. We foster research excellence and pursue discoveries in metabolic diseases, with experts working together in collaborative teams. Come and join us! •\tWe believe in a strong scientific commitment and reproducible findings to contribute to the way of thinking in diabetes research. •\tOur vision is to translate fundamental science to the clinic by a collaborative effort between scientists, physicians and the industry. Date limite : open till filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) PhD student-Cancer biology - Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) Faculté de Médecine The Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) at the Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB), led by Panagiotis (Takis) Karras, is seeking motivated researchers to undertake a PhD in cancer research. The candidate will focus on a project to better characterize the drivers of cancer metastasis, profile the inter- and intra-tumor heterogeneity and plasticity combining mouse models and clinical samples. The successful applicant will join the ULB Faculty of Medicine and the Institute Jules Bordet within the campus. Date limite : until the position is filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Postdoctoral researcher - Cancer biology Faculté de Médecine The Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) at the Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB), led by Panagiotis (Takis) Karras, is seeking talented a postdoc with a recent PhD or MD/PhD and experience in Cancer Biology/Biochemistry/Molecular Biology. The candidate will focus on a project to better characterize the drivers of cancer metastasis, profile the inter- and intra-tumor heterogeneity and plasticity combining mouse models and clinical samples. The successful applicant will join the ULB Faculty of Medicine and the Institute Jules Bordet within the campus. Date limite : until the position is filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Bioinformatician - Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) Faculté de Médecine The Cancer Ecosystems and Metastasis Laboratory (CEMLab) at the Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB), led by Panagiotis (Takis) Karras, is seeking for a skilled bioinformatician with experience in single-cell multi-omics. The candidate will focus on projects to better characterize the drivers of cancer metastasis, profile the inter- and intra-tumor heterogeneity and plasticity combining mouse models and clinical samples. Applicants should demonstrate expertise in programming languages (Python and/or R) as well as experience working with high-performance computing clusters. The successful applicant will join the ULB Faculty of Medicine and the Institute Jules Bordet within the campus. Date limite : Applications will be accepted until the position is filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Postdoctoral Scientist - Full-time position at the Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory in Brussels Faculté de Médecine Molecular mechanisms of obesity-associated liver cancer Date limite : open until filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Post-doctoral fellow molecular biology/immunology Faculté de Médecine ULB Center for Research in Immunology (U-CRI) Date limite : till filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Full time position : Research Assistant/Lab Organisation Faculté de Médecine Laboratory of Signal Transduction and Metabolism Date limite : open until filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Full-time technician position Faculté de Médecine ERC Funded project - Laboratory of Signal Transduction and Metabolism Date limite : open until filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Full-time Postdoctoral Scientist position Faculté de Médecine Molecular mechanisms of Metabolic Diseases Date limite : open until filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) PhD Student Full-time position Faculté de Médecine TELEVIE Funded project Liver inflammation and cancer in obesity at the Signal Transduction & Metabolism Laboratory Date limite : open until filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Postdoctoral Scientist - JDRF funded project - Molecular mechanisms of autoimmune diabetes Faculté de Médecine The Signal Transduction and Metabolism Laboratory led by Dr Esteban Gurzov is seeking highly motivated post-doctoral researchers to develop novel methods to diagnose type 1 diabetes, and to explore the pathophysiological mechanisms contributing to autoimmune diabetes. The successful applicant will join the Laboratoire de Gastroentérologie Expérimental et Endotools/ULB Faculty of Medicine (www.stmlaboratoy.com), characterised by an impressive track record in research excellence. Project description: The project will take advantage of human iPSC, diabetes cell models, mouse models, pharmacological approaches and human specimens to determine the molecular mechanisms by which tyrosine phosphatases contribute to the development of autoimmune diabetes and to explore novel approaches for combating type 1 diabetes. Lire l'annonce (pdf) FULL-TIME POSTDOCTORAL SCIENTIST POSITION Faculté de Médecine ERC Funded project Bioinformatician for obesity-associated liver cancer SIGNAL TRANSDUCTION & METABOLISM LABORATORY Date limite : open until filled Lire l'annonce (pdf) Mis à jour le 4 juillet 2025 Vous êtes Futur·e étudiant·e Parents Doctorant·e Étudiant·e de l'ULB Chercheuse, Chercheur Alumni Journaliste Entreprise Actrice, acteur de l'enseignement Pensionné·e de l'ULB Membre du personnel de l'ULB À propos Offre de formation S'inscrire à l'ULB Aides, services et accompagnement Vie sur les campus Formation des enseignant·es Formation continue Université Inter-Âges L'ULB à Charleroi L'ULB s'engage Faq et support Actualités et Agenda Annuaire de l'ULB Secours et sécurité Facultés, instituts et écoles Faculté de Philosophie et Sciences sociales Faculté de Lettres, Traduction et Communication Faculté de Droit et de Criminologie Solvay Brussels School of Economics and Management Faculté de Psychologie, des Sciences de l’Éducation et de Logopédie Faculté d'Architecture La Cambre Horta Faculté des Sciences École polytechnique de Bruxelles Faculté de Médecine École de Santé publique Faculté des Sciences de la Motricité humaine Faculté de Pharmacie École de Traduction et Interprétation ISTI - Cooremans École de Bioingénierie de Bruxelles (Environnement-Bioindustries-Agriculture) Pôle Santé Institut d'Études européennes ULB Langues Pôl